      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. Dead/unused code copied from a base class (generic `E` fields that won't compile, unused helpers)\n2. `__super_*` methods with no bodies (compile errors)\n3. Masses of unrelated utility methods that obscure the actual test intent\n4. The test exits immediately because `isRemoveSupported()` returns `true`\n\nI'll write a clean, focused version that strips all the noise while preserving identical runtime behavior.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes ~400 lines of dead code (unused helpers, uncompilable `E`-generic fields, `__super_*` method stubs) and replaces it with a focused ~130-line class that exposes only the infrastructure actually needed by `testUnsupportedRemove`."
